date_type = 1
edits_description = "The background was removed and only the mask was used."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_7d811")
blurb = "Depicts the kabuki actor Ichikawa Danjūrō VII playing the role of Endō Musha Morichika. In the play, Morichika is obsessed with a married noblewoman, and in an attempt to murder her husband, kills her instead. As repentance he becomes the renowned Buddhist monk Mongaku.

The mask which the man is holding is the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hannya]Hannya[/url], a Noh theater mask representing a jealous female demon.

Several verses are inscribed on the print. The one on the left is by Ichikawa Sanshō, reading:

[i]In the spring field,
I cross the mist,
perhaps to revel.[/i]

The one on the right is by Goryūtei Tokushō:

[i]The edge of the mountain
draws mist,
iridescent.
In the hazy shadow,
Lovers embrace.[/i]"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
